.Dd July 9, 2026
.Dt XTC_FSM 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_fsm_start ,
.Nm xtc_fsm_stop ,
.Nm xtc_fsm_join ,
.Nm xtc_fsm_pid ,
.Nm xtc_fsm_send ,
.Nm xtc_fsm_call ,
.Nm xtc_fsm_reply
.Nd gen_statem-style finite state machine as a process
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.In xtc_fsm.h
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_fsm_start "xtc_loop_t *loop" "const xtc_fsm_callbacks_t *cb" "void *state" "int initial_state" "const xtc_fsm_opts_t *opts" "xtc_fsm_t **out"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_fsm_stop "xtc_fsm_t *fsm"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_fsm_join "xtc_fsm_t *fsm" "int64_t timeout_ns"
.Ft xtc_pid_t
.Fn xtc_fsm_pid "const xtc_fsm_t *fsm"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_fsm_send "xtc_pid_t target" "const void *ev" "size_t len"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_fsm_call "xtc_pid_t target" "const void *req" "size_t req_size" "void **out_reply" "size_t *out_size" "int64_t timeout_ns"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_fsm_reply "xtc_fsm_call_t *call" "const void *reply" "size_t size"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm xtc_fsm
family is a
.Xr gen_statem 3 Ns -style
finite state machine that runs as its own
.Xr xtc_proc 3 :
a disciplined loop over
.Fn xtc_recv
that dispatches each event to the caller's
.Fn event
callback for the current state and acts on the returned
.Vt xtc_fsm_result_t .
It standardizes the three features hand-rolled C switch machines almost
always get wrong:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Sy state_enter :
the
.Fn enter
callback runs on every state change, so entry actions live in one place.
.It
.Sy postponed events :
an event returned as
.Dv XTC_FSM_POSTPONE
is stashed and REPLAYED, oldest first, after the next
.Dv XTC_FSM_NEXT
transition, ahead of fresh events.
.It
.Sy state timeouts :
a result with
.Va state_timeout_ns No > 0
arms a timeout for the resulting state; if it fires first a synthetic
state-timeout event is delivered to
.Fn event
with
.Fa msg No == NULL
and
.Fa len No == 0
.Pq Dv XTC_FSM_IS_STATE_TIMEOUT .
Any real event cancels a pending state timeout.
.El
.Pp
.Fn xtc_fsm_start
spawns the machine on
.Fa loop
in
.Fa initial_state
.Pq Fn enter No is called for it first
and returns a handle in
.Fa out .
.Fn xtc_fsm_stop
asks the machine to stop (non-blocking; runs
.Fn terminate ,
then the proc exits);
.Fn xtc_fsm_join
waits for exit and frees the handle.
.Fn xtc_fsm_pid
returns the machine's pid.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_fsm_send
delivers an asynchronous, fire-and-forget event (arrives with
.Fa call No == NULL ) .
.Fn xtc_fsm_call
delivers a synchronous request and blocks until the machine replies or
.Fa timeout_ns
elapses; on success
.Fa out_reply
receives a heap buffer the caller releases with
.Xr xtc_free 3 .
Inside
.Fn event ,
when
.Fa call
is non-NULL the callback answers it exactly once with
.Fn xtc_fsm_reply .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
All functions returning
.Vt int
return
.Dv XTC_OK
on success or a negative
.Dv XTC_E_*
code;
.Fn xtc_fsm_call
returns
.Dv XTC_E_AGAIN
on timeout and must be called from within a process.
.Fn xtc_fsm_join
returns
.Dv XTC_E_AGAIN
on timeout, leaving the handle valid to join again.
.Fn xtc_fsm_pid
returns the machine's pid, or
.Dv XTC_PID_NONE
for a NULL handle.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_svr 3 ,
.Xr xtc_proc 3 ,
.Xr xtc_supervisor 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
.Sh HISTORY
Appeared in xtc 1.10.
